}
```
This is the same logic shape (bisect on a bit) duplicated twice. It's a clear Duplicated Code smell — could be a small helper `bisect(bit, minRef, maxRef)`. But it's only two instances and arguably clearer inlined. This is a judgement-call baseline smell. The original code ALSO had this duplication (single loop doing both). Actually the original loop did both lat and lon in one loop, so it had a similar repeated shape but combined. The new version splits into two near-identical loops — this slightly increases the duplication surface. I'll note it as a minor Duplicated Code judgement call.

